# {{ app_name }}

{{ description }}

A Kotlin ([Micronaut](https://micronaut.io/)) app on the [swhurl platform](https://github.com/samclement/swhurl-platform), made from the [swhurl Kotlin template](https://github.com/samclement/swhurl-app-template-kotlin). Every push to `main` is checked, published to `ghcr.io/<owner>/{{ app_name }}` and deployed to staging; production changes through **Promote to prod**. What the image must provide, the checks and the dependency updates: the [template's guide](https://github.com/samclement/swhurl-app-template-kotlin#readme). What the app needs from the platform: [`swhurl.yaml`](swhurl.yaml).

{% if kind == 'web' -%}
An HTTP service: `HttpController.kt` answers on port 8080; the platform probes `GET /healthz`.
{%- else -%}
A background worker with no web address: `Worker.kt` runs `work()` every `WORK_INTERVAL_MS` (default a minute).
{%- endif %}
{%- if database == 'sqlite' %} It keeps its data in SQLite (`Database.kt`): on the platform the file is `/data/app.db` (`DATABASE_PATH`) on a volume that outlives the pod, backed up nightly; staging and production each have their own. Change the schema by adding `migrations/NNN_name.sql` (applied once each, in order, at startup); never edit one that has run.{% endif %}

## Local development

Needs a JDK 25 (Gradle downloads everything else):

```bash
./gradlew run                           # the agent stays off locally (the image loads it)
{%- if kind == 'web' %}
curl http://localhost:8080/healthz
{%- endif %}
./gradlew check                         # compile and tests, as CI does
```
{%- if database == 'sqlite' %}

Locally the database is `app.db` in this directory (ignored by Git); delete it to start again.
{%- endif %}
